# dev server — `npm run dev` → bin/streamo.js --env-file env/dev.env
#
# ⚠️ THIS DOES NOT CURRENTLY SERVE public/. Verified 2026-08-04, twice, from
# a clean tree. It binds :8080 and serves the root index and public/streamo/,
# then dies. Read this before spending an evening on it — one already went.
#
# WHY. `public/mounts.json` pins a `key` on every `ours: true` mount. Those
# keys were derived from the PRODUCTION identity. This file's identity
# (dev/dev/1) derives different ones — all five mismatch, checked:
#
#   streamo/          pinned 02b1d2ee…   dev derives 027166c1…
#   apps/flashcards/  pinned 03e15f71…   dev derives 03c68553…
#   apps/explorer/    pinned 03d6b60d…   dev derives 0361e85c…
#   apps/todomvc/     pinned 02ba9dc8…   dev derives 025f675a…
#   apps/styles/      pinned 020869c4…   dev derives 0334687a…
#
# So FolderRecord.writeMany throws on the first mount it reaches:
#   "derived child pubkey … doesn't match mount target … for 'apps/explorer/'"
# Whether you see a 200 first is a race — it depends on whether the web server
# binds before writeMany gets there.
#
# AND THE FAILURE HIDES ITSELF. The crash kills the process mid-archive-write,
# leaving .streamo/<key>.bin a few bytes longer than anything that loads back.
# The NEXT start then dies in tieredArchiveSync with "refusing to overwrite …
# another process is racing this one" — pointing at contention that does not
# exist. That is the error you will actually see, and it is downstream.
# Recover by moving .streamo/0291eb29….bin aside; it re-syncs.
#
# THE FIX IS A DESIGN CALL, WHICH IS WHY IT ISN'T MADE HERE. Three shapes:
#
#   1. Don't pin keys on `ours: true` mounts. They're derivable from whoever
#      signs — pinning one hardcodes an identity into a committed file, which
#      is the whole bug. `apps/grove/` already has no key and is the only
#      mount that can't cause this. Changes prod's Record structure, so it
#      wants David.
#   2. Run dev with the credentials that own those keys. Works today; means a
#      dev server that can author production Records, which is its own problem.
#   3. Serve prod read-only instead of authoring: drop STREAMO_FILES and set
#      STREAMO_HOME_KEY=<prod key>. Supported today (`--home-key` is relay-only
#      and mutually exclusive with --files). Gives you prod's content locally,
#      but edits to public/ won't appear — which may not be what "dev" means.
#
# Until one of those is chosen, `npm run dev` starts and dies.
#
STREAMO_NAME=streamo-dev
STREAMO_USERNAME=dev
STREAMO_PASSWORD=dev
STREAMO_KEY_ITERATIONS=1
STREAMO_FEED=streamo.dev
STREAMO_FILES=public
STREAMO_WEB=8080
